            "id": "ann_1",
            "type": "note",
            "text": "ParticleStateTOP — Visualize POP Attributes as Textures\n\nParticleStateTOP reads GPU particle data and encodes it as a\n2D texture. Each pixel = one particle. Three instances show:\n  • Position (XYZ → RGB)\n  • Velocity (scaled by 0.2 for visibility)\n  • Color (RGBA particle color attribute)\n\nUseful for debugging POP chains or feeding particle data\ninto TOP shader processing pipelines.",
